{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1478348-2e-confussion-about-inverosimile-setting","id":1478348,"title":"2E Confussion about inverosimile setting","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-04-09T06:00:50-07:00","id":1478348,"title":"2E Confussion about inverosimile setting","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> <br /> I have read the mechanical details on the Purviews and Knacks sections of Scion, but I am really at fault for barely skimming the world lore. I ask the forums to explain to me: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Are the gods publicly known and revered?</b><br /> I keep finding random paragraphs about secrecy and history being lost (how if you can ask your gods about things that happened?) but also that traffic controllers need to coordinate heaven residences and Chinese air traffic, that Lanka exist and government tried to invade, that some creatures have a public social network, etc.</li> <li><b>How does the setting explain the fact that history could have not gone the same if gods exist?</b><br /> This is the part that seems the least consistent to me. Some nations would not exist at all, some buildings, monuments, people, technology would have arrived (if at all) through different channels.</li> <li><b>What role, if any does monotheism play on the setting?</b><br /> I see the Americas were conquered by the Spaniards... But some of the things the Spaniard did (e.g. suppressing &quot;heathen&quot; religions) would make no sense if the native deities exist and intervene. The mere existence of SPAIN as a nation will make little sense if the Theoi were active in the Roman Empire.<br /> <br /> Christianity-influenced thought played a large role in European science during centuries, some historical and social issues are Christianity derived: homosexuality decried as a sin, having as many children as you physically could, the Crusades and the partition of Arab territories, &quot;evangelizing&quot; the Americas, modern day Americans self image and voting patterns, etc.</li> </ol><br /> Essentially, I find the mechanical part interesting, but the setting as a whole lacking verisimilitude. It requires some heavy mental gymnastics to pretend the deities exist in some form and intervene at some level, while having a world that looks like current day Earth plus Scions.<br /> <br /> Again, this might be me misinterpreting and there might be a set of good explanations, that I am missing, but I have yet to find those.<br /> <br /> Thanks for your time and attention,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 04-09-2022, 01:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T06:51:17-07:00","id":1478353,"title":"","content":"We got this discussion few times already - here is most comprehensive topic about it on forum -<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1274898-everyday-life-with-gods\"><b>Everyday life with Gods</b></a><br /> <br /> Myself, I run the game with <b>'Gods in Hiding'</b> Hack, officially called as <b>Iron </b>or<b> Heroic</b><b> Evidance Dial </b>( see <b>Scion 2E Companion - Mysteries of the World </b>book on more ). <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1275725-2e-setting-hack-gods-in-hiding-and-new-mythic-age\">Here is our hack topic in all the glory</a>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-09-2022, 02:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T07:27:02-07:00","id":1478358,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the link. It still comes to the point, the stated setting is not self-consistent.<br /> <br /> Mage the Awakening did something (to my eyes) amazing with the <b>Aponoia </b>condition.<br /> <br /> Essentially, when mages awaken (transforming from normal human to mage), they go to the Supernal: the platonic realm of ideas, the blueprint of the universe itself. Interacting with the Supernal should only awake the person, but any modification there, is retroactive here. There are in-game examples of an Archmage (uber tier mage, that undergoes a second awakening at some point in their lives), coming back utterly baffled by this &quot;Christianity&quot; thing being so prominent.<br /> <br /> A mechanical simile to <b>Aponoia</b>, a retroactive-continuity-adjustment would smooth some (but not all) of Scion faults.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 04-09-2022, 01:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T08:25:11-07:00","id":1478364,"title":"","content":"I think you may be right, but its also possible you are wrong.<br /> <br /> My point is, the christian god is also real and people in Europe abandoned largely their beliefs in the other pantheons in favor of the christian god, as they did in our world.<br /> To many (and I mean like 1/2 of the world population) the gods are real and they walk among us all the time (like in Scion), the difference is that you don\u00b4t believe in it, and in Scion you do. The Christian god would give their followers power enough to fight the others, and with technology in their side the other gods would be defeated (as their civilizations did in our world). The result would be basically the same world, but with a bit more magic and a bit less technology, at least if the general population access to magic is restricted (not only monetary, but due to risks and other kinds of difficulties).<br /> <br /> On a more fantastic version of the setting, than for sure you would never have any of the modern nations the way they are, with divisions more related to the gods they follow and less about other politics. You would hardly have any colonized countries, as their gods would protect their populations from the other gods, with little interference of technological powers (fire at first, all the way to guns and bombs). Not to mention technology itself that would not evolve as much as it did in our world, just because magic is available (who would fund a airplane inventor if the rich people had access to magic carpets?).<br /> <br /> Its a very interesting discussion, it goes around Lord of the Rings and how the ages were so long and with so little advancement (or change in general), and the simple answer is Elves and Magic. Immortals don\u00b4t like change, we know it because people don\u00b4t like change when we get old, and with magic available, even in so little portions as in Middle Earth, it would be enough to prevent technology to advance as fast as it did in our world. In Scion we have immortals and we have magic, so we would probably be in the same situation, with a roughly 5000 years long middle age since the first empires risen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T08:37:23-07:00","id":1478366,"title":"","content":"The canon world doesn't work, at least not for me. You either gave to change it to something that recognizes that borders and cultures are completely different (do the Gods allow the settlers and colonists to brutalize their people? If not, that changes a lot right there), or say the Gods have been away and are now returning - which is 1st edition's approach. I just don't think that powerful beings would allow things to progress as they have, with monotheistic faiths all but burying their worship. Just look at the scope of the changes your players will make in the duration of a campaign - why assume that their divine parents (or other scions) would have been passive the last 2,000 years?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T09:27:11-07:00","id":1478375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1478348-2e-confussion-about-inverosimile-setting?p=1478358#post1478358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the link. It still comes to the point, the stated settings should is not self-consistent.<br /> <br /> Mage the Awakening did something (to my eyes) amazing with the <b>Aponoia </b>condition.<br /> <br /> Essentially, when mages awaken (transforming from normal human to mage), they go to the Supernal: the platonic realm of ideas, the blueprint of the universe itself. Interacting with the Supernal should only awake the person, but any modification there, is retroactive here. There are in-game examples of an Archmage (uber tier mage, that undergoes a second awakening at some point in their lives), coming back utterly baffled by this &quot;Christianity&quot; thing being so prominent.<br /> <br /> A mechanical simile to <b>Aponoia</b>, a retroactive-continuity-adjustment would smooth some (but not all) of Scion faults.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>There <i>does</i> appear to be something along the lines of Aponoia in <b>Scion</b> 2e; but it's restricted to the founding of a Pantheon, and the details about it haven't been revealed yet. I'm pretty sure that it's one of the things that <b>Scion: God</b> will address. <br /> <br /> What <i>is</i> known is that some Pantheons remember when other Pantheons weren't Pantheons yet; and that one of the steps of establishing a Pantheon involves writing its creation myth into the history of the World, retroactively making it true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T09:42:14-07:00","id":1478383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1478348-2e-confussion-about-inverosimile-setting?p=1478366#post1478366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The canon world doesn't work, at least not for me. You either gave to change it to something that recognizes that borders and cultures are completely different (do the Gods allow the settlers and colonists to brutalize their people? If not, that changes a lot right there), or say the Gods have been away and are now returning - which is 1st edition's approach. I just don't think that powerful beings would allow things to progress as they have, with monotheistic faiths all but burying their worship. Just look at the scope of the changes your players will make in the duration of a campaign - why assume that their divine parents (or other scions) would have been passive the last 2,000 years?</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of this is tied to the devs' stated hands-off policy when it comes to the Abrahamic religions: while they have very good reasons for said policy, and I'm not saying that it's wrong, one effect of it is that they're unable to address this particular issue in any real depth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T21:27:16-07:00","id":1478466,"title":"","content":"Essentially, it comes down to asking, &quot;if the Abrahamic religion(s) are real, why would they be more prevalent than the others?&quot; Worship doesn't make you stronger in Scion, so there's no reason why &quot;Capital G made the world in six days&quot; is any more valid than any other creation story (and &quot;all myths are true&quot; in Scion); Zeus is just as strong as ever, as are Odin, Tezcatlipoca, Amaterasu, and all the rest, and there's no compelling logic as to why they would allow their faithful to be led away or killed off without retaliating. Whatever God/Allah/Yahweh/Jehovah is, it can't be more special than all the other Gods, or that raises questions of &quot;then where did it come from?&quot;, and &quot;If it made everything, did it make pantheons of rival Gods just to humiliate them?&quot; It just doesn't work, and it's tne biggest hole in the canon game history from my perspective. There may be good reasons why OP hasn't addressed it, but that doesn't eliminate the problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-10T02:17:55-07:00","id":1478477,"title":"","content":"Not really. The point is, all myths are true, when Capital G create the world he didn't create the other gods because the other gods are not part of his myth.<br /> <br /> Capital G have more followers, what makes him more prone to fatebound what makes him more present in the world. The other gods have less followers, what makes them less prone to fatebinding, and so more absent, what makes them less powerful in the world.<br /> <br /> Also, Capital G took many of the mantles and titles of the other European gods (mainly the most powerful of them), Allfather, Sky Father, the one above all, the best of all (Optimus Maximus), the most powerful, etc. It is the kind of thing that takes the versatility and general power and presence of the other gods.<br /> <br /> Indeed Zeus is as powerful as ever, that's part of his myth, but in the final counting, he has about as many followers he had 3000 years ago (a few thousand people), while Capital G has many thousand times more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-10T05:26:18-07:00","id":1478484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1478348-2e-confussion-about-inverosimile-setting?p=1478466#post1478466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Essentially, it comes down to asking, &quot;if the Abrahamic religion(s) are real, why would they be more prevalent than the others?&quot; Worship doesn't make you stronger in Scion, so there's no reason why &quot;Capital G made the world in six days&quot; is any more valid than any other creation story (and &quot;all myths are true&quot; in Scion); Zeus is just as strong as ever, as are Odin, Tezcatlipoca, Amaterasu, and all the rest, and there's no compelling logic as to why they would allow their faithful to be led away or killed off without retaliating. Whatever God/Allah/Yahweh/Jehovah is, it can't be more special than all the other Gods, or that raises questions of &quot;then where did it come from?&quot;, and &quot;If it made everything, did it make pantheons of rival Gods just to humiliate them?&quot; It just doesn't work, and it's tne biggest hole in the canon game history from my perspective. There may be good reasons why OP hasn't addressed it, but that doesn't eliminate the problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Historically, the Abrahamic faiths won out because they simply appealed to more people and were far less linked to place or ethnic group (which is ironic because the faith which Christianity and Islam came from, Judaism, is profoundly tied to both a place and an ethnic group). The teachings of the later Jewish prophets and Christ were appealing and the restrictions on membership were few. <br /> <br /> Historically, most gods simply didn't go for the mass market. For many Greek cults you had to be born in a certain family or community to join. Many faiths never took slaves, former slaves, people who worked with their hands, the sick, the disfigured or the lame. Many cults were expensive to join. The cult of Mithras required being able to buy several bulls in order to be bathed in their blood. Many cults were restricted by sex. Christianity and Islam both loudly proclaimed they'd take anyone. Christianity specified &quot;For free and without cost.&quot; To join Islam you simply recited the Shahada and meant it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 04-10-2022, 06:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-10T05:29:46-07:00","id":1478485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1478348-2e-confussion-about-inverosimile-setting?p=1478477#post1478477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Capital G took many of the mantles and titles of the other European gods (mainly the most powerful of them), Allfather, Sky Father, the one above all, the best of all (Optimus Maximus), the most powerful, etc. It is the kind of thing that takes the versatility and general power and presence of the other gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did Capital G <b><i>stole</i></b> the Mantels of other Old Gods - or simply got the same ones? Is there only one Sky Father? Or maybe they are many Gods with this Mantle, with Capital G only one of them?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-10T08:24:33-07:00","id":1478492,"title":"","content":"As I understand it, \u201cSky Father\u201d isn't a Mantle; it's a Title. \u201cZeus\u201d is a Mantle. <br /> <br /> The difference, as I understand it, is that a Mantle is a god's position within a given Pantheon; when you take a Mantle, you become part of that Pantheon, and whoever had that Mantle before doesn't have it anymore. By contrast, a Title is more of a property of a Mantle: take the Mantle, and you get all of its Titles. On the other hand, while this makes a given Title unique <i>within</i> a Pantheon, a Title isn't unique <i>to</i> a Pantheon: multiple Pantheons can have their own Mantles that include a \u201cSky Father\u201d, with no conflict. <br /> <br /> But yes, a lot of religious conflict takes the form of appropriating Mantles: \u201cyour goddess Brigid is actually our Saint Brigitte\u201d, or some such. Mind you, this isn't unique to Christianity or Islam; the Shen, for instance, exist largely as they do due to extensive appropriation of local gods into a \u201cgreater whole\u201d. Indeed, it <i>might</i> be said that the Shen are to China as Christianity is to Europe and Islam is to the Middle East, and not be <i>too</i> far off the mark.<br /> <br /> Which brings up another point: the Abrahamic faiths are dominant\u2026 in the West and in the Middle East. But how dominant are they elsewhere? I'm pretty sure that the Shen, Kami, and Deva's respective religions haven't been crushed under the boot of the Abrahamic faiths; and the Orisha might be in a similar position, for all I know (as opposed to the Loa, who wouldn't exist <i>without</i> Christianity, and are arguably a subversion of the aforementioned appropriations).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 04-10-2022, 11:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-10T15:30:24-07:00","id":1478519,"title":"","content":"But that still leaves the question, &quot;Why would powerful, active Gods allow their mantles to be stolen in the first place?&quot; Scion is based around the premise that Gods are all real, active, powerful beings that openly aid their worshippers, creating Scions and manifesting in some form all over the world, not just in their &quot;native lands&quot;. Magical creatures exist (Kitsune, Alfar, Jotun, Nymphs, and so on), and the mystical and fantastic are both real and far more obvious and prevalent than in our own world. This isn't reality; it's supposed to be a game about the Gods of all faiths being present and active in a magical world. Reducing it to &quot;the same as ours because Capital G stole their mantles&quot; seems to me to miss out on the depth of the possibilities in the setting.<br /> (To prevent issues - I know real world faiths are real to their faithful; I'm discussing the game here)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5627,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","user":"Purple Snit","date":".  corrected spelling and prose 04-11-2022, 01:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-13T16:20:22-07:00","id":1478803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1478348-2e-confussion-about-inverosimile-setting?p=1478519#post1478519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that still leaves the question, &quot;Why would powerful, active Gods allow their mantles to be stolen in the first place?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt &quot;allowed&quot; has anything to do with it. While gods might struggle over things, perhaps even violently, the end result for the people on the ground is &quot;this is how it always was,&quot; or at least not seeing the direct divine conflict.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-14T18:07:05-07:00","id":1478879,"title":"","content":"My personal take is that The World (Scion's setting) is akin to a multi-faceted gem, and exactly how many facets the PCs are aware of is dependent on a number of factors including (but not limited to) the various Setting Dials the GM uses, which pantheon(s) the PCs are a part of, how many other pantheons they interact with, what power level they are at (Hero, Demi, God), what interaction they have with Titans (or Dragons or whatever else is out there), etc. And everyone's mileage may vary. <br /> <br /> (I kind of want to try to work up a setting using the idea of the ur-city - Metropolis, Babylon, The City of Mists, whatever you want to call it - where it is to gods what Alan Moore's Top Ten was to superheros. All of them are there out in the open, with their Heroes engaged in every single urban fantasy adventure trope all at once.)<br /> <br /> ((Likewise, I also want to experiment with high fantasy alternative history where you have these kingdoms that feel like that pantheon's mythic age meshed with later periods and technology. Mediterranean city states that combine mythical and classical Greece with Renaissance Italy and bits of the Romantic era, for example. Or a Camelot that meshes classic Welsh/Britton with aspects of medieval fantasy and Tudor England. And so on. ))<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-14T18:31:15-07:00","id":1478881,"title":"","content":"There isn't a &quot;right&quot; or &quot; wrong&quot; way to play it, but I've always been an fan of alternate histories and timelines in my gaming, so this to me seemed like a perfect chance to go wild with the &quot;what if?&quot; of it. You can certainly make a game out of &quot;Capital G stole the mantles, and the Gods are at war trying to stop the usurper and get their mantles back&quot;, which could be pretty cool if played well. I just prefer a more overt &quot;the world ain't the same&quot; take on things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-14T21:48:19-07:00","id":1478891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1478348-2e-confussion-about-inverosimile-setting?p=1478881#post1478881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There isn't a &quot;right&quot; or &quot; wrong&quot; way to play it, but I've always been an fan of alternate histories and timelines in my gaming, so this to me seemed like a perfect chance to go wild with the &quot;what if?&quot; of it. You can certainly make a game out of &quot;Capital G stole the mantles, and the Gods are at war trying to stop the usurper and get their mantles back&quot;, which could be pretty cool if played well. I just prefer a more overt &quot;the world ain't the same&quot; take on things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tbh that's fair. I am going to guess--and this is entirely hypothesis--that the current rather vague and occasionally self-contradictory setting is mainly because the point isn't really that you're living in a world where all myths are true, or at least many more are verifiable. Let's face it, there are people today who believe in gods who created the world, and have the interests of their people at heart, and yet... *gestures outside at the everything*. It's kind of disrespectful to religions today to create a setting where their lot in life and place in the world is better because their gods are real (and unspoken yet implied: &quot;because in our own world your gods do not exist.&quot;) For believers, the gods are present, real, and the world exists as it does today with them in it. To present a world where higher powers shape the world differently is to presume knowing the gods' wills better than they do.<br /> <br /> So it's actually kind of the point that the rough shape of the world is very much like the one we live in now. Wordcount for a new setting and an alternate timeline where the will of the gods has openly dictated the lines on the maps would be really interesting, but if you're trying to keep things to a slim, non-threatening core* and supplements then the current approach of &quot;assume it's pretty much like the real world, except where it needs not to be for your game&quot; is ideal. The writers don't need to spend a lot of wordcount on a whole alternate history that makes the world radically different, because that's a lot of effort spent on things that aren't important and really runs the risk of getting future writers bogged down in the weeds. <br /> <br /> * I love Exalted Third Edition, I really do, but I also understand that the absolute bullet-stopper of a tome can make potential players back down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-15T07:51:49-07:00","id":1478907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1478348-2e-confussion-about-inverosimile-setting?p=1478891#post1478891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's face it, there are people today who believe in gods who created the world, and have the interests of their people at heart, and yet... *gestures outside at the everything*. It's kind of disrespectful to religions today to create a setting where their lot in life and place in the world is better because their gods are real (and unspoken yet implied: &quot;because in our own world your gods do not exist.&quot;)</div> </div> </div> </div>This is, for the record, the approach we take as writers. If anyone wants to know why The World looks the way it does while Gods are active in it, talk to people who already live in that world. Talk to people who've witnessed miracles, encountered living saints, visited sorcerers, and spoken to the dead. They aren't that hard to find. I barely go out and I run into at least one a week.<br /> <br /> But the quicker way is just to take that one element of Scion as a given and enjoy the game as a game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Scion 2E</b> Freelancer: <i>Origin; Hero; Demigod; God; Mythical Denizens; Mysteries of the World; Saints &amp; Monsters; No Gods, No Masters; Once &amp; Future, Realms of Magic &amp; Mystery</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/369-geoffrey","name":"Geoffrey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-15T10:50:24-07:00","id":1478915,"title":"","content":"I understand that there is a need to avoid upsetting people in the real world - implying their deities aren't &quot;real&quot; enough. But Scion isn't reality; there are going to be PCs who are the literal children of the Gods, possessed of the ability to fly, control weather, influence hearts and minds directly, raise the dead, and so on. No-one (I hope) is saying that this happens in reality. And the Scions (and their parents) of a world where Odin/Kaglulik/Oshosi/etc. have literally and tangibly walked among people and had children with them, and gifted them the power to do supernatural things, would look very different from our own, IMO. Obviously, either I'm in a minority, or it's just a topic that is too touchy to pursue, and that's fine. I just wanted to express my view.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}